# Mutation table for the third WriteErrors gate: POST /api/v1/dedup/rescore.
#
# Format: NAME | FILE | PERL_EXPRESSION      (see scripts/mutation-matrix.sh)
# Run:
#   scripts/mutation-matrix.sh \
#     --pkg ./internal/server/handlers/dedup/ \
#     --table scripts/mutation-tables/dedup-score-config-endpoint.muts
#
# WHY THIS TABLE IS ITS OWN FILE. PR #3058 changed RescoreResult's contract so
# a nil error can accompany WriteErrors > 0, and updated two of the three
# callers. This endpoint was the third — and it is the one every partial-re-band
# message tells the operator to run, so a 200 here means the remedy reported
# success having done half the job. That is the shape of defect this repo keeps
# shipping: a 200 OK carrying the failure in its body.

M01 answer 200 on a re-band that failed to write | internal/server/handlers/dedup/handler.go | s/\tif result\.WriteErrors > 0 \{/\tif false {/
